The contents of the `checker/` directory are derived from nanoda_lib at commit
ddfac2bf5a7b56cb46e141494427ff3dd55963c7 (v0.4.10-beta), imported with its
full upstream history via `git subtree`. The upstream license text is retained
verbatim at `checker/LICENSE`.

Modifications by the nanodatg authors to the imported sources are described in
`DECISIONS.md` and are, in summary: threading proof certificates through the
definitional-equality and inference paths so that the checker emits derivations
in the trusted `kernel/` crate rather than returning a bare accept/reject
verdict.

To see the modifications as a diff against upstream:

    git remote add nanoda-upstream https://github.com/ammkrn/nanoda_lib
    git fetch nanoda-upstream
    git diff nanoda-upstream/master -- checker/
